 ```

+For SM120, build the CUDA extension for the device architecture:
+
+```bash
+DEEP_SELECT_CUDA_ARCHS=120a NVCC_THREADS=1 MAX_JOBS=6 \
+  python -m pip install --no-build-isolation --no-deps .
+```
+
+The SM120 specialization in `csrc/sm120_topk512.cu` supports BF16 inputs,
+int32 indices, `topk <= 512`, `sorted=False`, `sorted_index=False`, and
+`return_value=False`. Its 256-thread, single-resident-block configuration
+uses two TMA load buffers to fit the SM120 shared-memory limit. Input row
+strides must be multiples of 1024 bytes and vocabulary width must be below
+2²³. Equal-score ties do not require prefix-index selection.
+
 ## Usage

 ```python
